From e574fa0224abbb60c193ee9b5c935dd8e0fd7529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:01:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] [flutter_tools] Vendor code_assets 1.0.0 and hooks_runner
 1.0.1

Class: local workaround (carry mechanism; no functional change).

flutter_tools 3.41.9 pins code_assets 1.0.0 and hooks_runner 1.0.1 from
pub.dev. Neither knows the ppc64 architecture, and flutter_tools cannot
map TargetPlatform.linux_ppc64 to a native-assets target without it. The
fix belongs in dart-lang/native, but the tool has to carry it until then,
and the flutter package must build without fetching patched packages.

This adds the two pub.dev archives, unmodified, under third_party/pkg
(lib/, pubspec.yaml, LICENSE, README.md, CHANGELOG.md; sha256 and
upstream tag in third_party/pkg/README.flutter-port) and points
flutter_tools' dependency_overrides at them. The next commit applies the
ppc64 change to them. Pub accepts the archives' `resolution: workspace`
for path overrides, so the pubspecs stay as published.

third_party/ is gclient-managed and ignores everything by default, so
third_party/.gitignore allow-lists pkg/.

The overrides change the pubspec, so `flutter update-packages
--verify-only` will report a stale PUBSPEC CHECKSUM; that check is not
part of building or running the tool.
